    "title": "Ride into Route 66 Summerfest - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Cielo Rodriguez ,\n22 hours ago The annual Albuquerque community event revs up the celebration with a century of music and parade of 100 cars. FOR DIEGO LUCERO, deputy director of the City of Albuquerque’s Department of Arts & Culture, this year’s Route 66 Summerfest will feel like walking through the evolution of the Mother Road. With four stages of live music, the lineup of acts will span every musical era over the past century, ranging from early jazz and 1960s rockabilly to 1980s yacht-rock headliners the Docksiders. “Summerfest is a community celebration,” he says. We talked with Lucero for a preview of the July 18 event that’s jam-packed with classic music and even more classic rides. Read full article",
